  "text_md": "Table II:\n\n|                            | sandwich        | brickwork       |\n|----------------------------|-----------------|-----------------|\n| excitation energy Ea       | 2.522 4 0.014eV | 2.565 + 0.010eV |\n| excitation energy Eb       | 2.523 4 0.014eV | 2.561 + 0.010eV |\n| excitonic coupling Verc    | 0.25 + 0.017 eV |                 |\n| center-center distance Rab |                 | 8.33 +          |\n| angle between long axes    | 6.0 + 1.70      | 34.0 + 4.00     |\n| angle between short axes   |                 | 122.0 + 3.90    |\n| distance of centers charge |                 | 7.57            |\n\n## V FIGURE CAPTIONS:\n\n## Figure 1:\n\nThe atom numbering for PIC is shown as it is used to tabulate the parameters\n\n## Figure 2:\n\nThe experimental absorption spectrum4 of monomeric PIC (dots) is compared with a calculated spectrum (full line) from the displaced oscillator model. The calculated spectrum was shifted to reproduce the absorption maximum at 1910Ocm-1\n\n## Figure 3:\n\nStarting from a sandwich (a) or brickwork (b) structure relative stable dimer configurations evolved. The figure shows representative snapshots.",
